==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|chillblain}}

===Etymology===
From {{com|en|chill|blain|lit=cold sore}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/t͡ʃɪlbleɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vanderdecken-chilblain.wav|Audio (UK)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An itchy purple red [[inflammation]] of the [[skin]], especially of the [[hand]]s, [[feet]] and [[ear]]s, occurring when [[capillary|capillaries]] below the skin are damaged by exposure to cold weather (but do not [[freeze]], which would lead to [[frostbite]] instead).
#: {{syn|en|erythema pernio|pernio}}
#* {{RQ:Austen Emma|I|3|passage=Mrs. Goddard’s school was in high repute—and very deservedly; for Highbury was reckoned a particularly healthy spot: she had an ample house and garden, gave the children plenty of wholesome food, let them run about a great deal in the summer, and in winter dressed their '''chilblains''' with her own hands.}}
#* {{RQ:Charlotte Bronte Jane Eyre|chapter=VII|page=105|text=Our clothing was insufficient to protect us from the severe cold: we had no boots, the snow got into our shoes and melted there; our ungloved hands became numbed and covered with '''chilblains''', as were our feet{{...}}}}

